CONCEPT
  product: Mezz, a 412-store coffeehouse chain built on the Middle Place doctrine
  angle:   the chain's operational language is birth order. Queue position, cup
           accuracy and seat assignment are all downstream of where you came in
           the family. Every promise on the page is a slight delivered in the
           passive voice.
  demo:    Store Console for Store No. 2 of 3 (floor plan, cup printer, queue rail)

DESIGN DIRECTION
  style:   risograph two-ink print, newsprint daylight mode. Two inks only, hard
           misregistration instead of shadow, CSS halftone screens, knockout
           section headers, registration-mark bullets, hatched section seams.
  palette: primary #0B49C8 (federal blue), accent #FF4FA3 (fluorescent pink),
           bg #F1ECDF (newsprint), fg/ink #141414, muted #8B8574
  fonts:   display 'Archivo Black', body 'Work Sans'
  anti-sameness: checked against the last 7 entries (microfilm carrel, moulded
           console shell, gallery wall labels, intaglio banknote, vitreous enamel
           signage, cyanotype blueprint, illuminated manuscript). No collision on
           style, palette or font pair. Neither typeface appears in the last 7.
           ui-ux-pro-max returned Exaggerated Minimalism / Rubik + Nunito Sans /
           #2563EB + #F97316, which was discarded as too close to a generic SaaS
           default; palette and fonts were derived custom for the riso conceit.

